Ignore a project settings file

Records that snouty must ignore the settings file at PATH, also after its
content changes. To use the file again, run `settings trust`.

Examples:
  snouty settings deny
  snouty settings deny path/to/.snouty.toml

Usage: snouty settings deny [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          The project settings file
          
          [default: .snouty.toml]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
